  0 failed. `ruff check --select F` is clean on the changed files.
- Still not verified: a live reasoning run on Lakebase or Delta with a removal rule.

## Fix: Simple Remove rule could not be saved (no THEN relationship)

### Context
A Simple (IF-THEN) rule with action `Remove` could not be saved. The user had to put a
relationship under THEN, but the editor refused it: "Add to THEN" was hidden for any element
already selected in IF, and selecting a relationship as THEN moved it out of IF and turned its
endpoints into THEN classes, which validation rejects for a retraction. In Remove mode a
relationship must be able to sit in both IF (to bind its variables) and THEN (the triple to
delete), and its endpoints must bind from IF.

### Changes
1. `src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-if-then.js`:
   - `_canAddToThen(elementId)` (new): in assert mode, unchanged rule (an element already used in
     IF or THEN cannot be added to THEN); in Remove mode, only relationships not already in THEN.
   - `_showContextMenu`: the "Add to THEN" item uses `_canAddToThen`.
   - `_selectLink`: in Remove mode the relationship stays in IF when added to THEN, and its
     endpoints are bound in IF (`endpointSide`). Assert mode is unchanged.
   - `saveRule`: a Remove rule without a THEN part gets an explicit message pointing to
     "Add to THEN".
2. `src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html`: the Remove hint now says
   to right-click a relationship and choose "Add to THEN", and that its endpoints bind from IF.
3. `tests/units/front/test_if_then_remove_editor.py` (new, 9 tests): runs `IfThenModule` under
   node against a stubbed DOM. Remove mode: a condition relationship can be added to THEN, stays
   in IF, endpoints bind in IF, a class cannot be added to THEN. Assert mode: unchanged behaviour.

### Modified files
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-if-then.js
- src/front/templates/partials/ontology/_ontology_business_rules.html
- tests/units/front/test_if_then_remove_editor.py (new)
- changelogs/v0.10.0/benoitcayladbx_2026-11-26.log

